ate_margin_vs_hist":-0.047599424974699045,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":100.0,"_gate_piotroski":7,"_gp_piotroski":true,"_score_piotroski":77.8,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":-0.025451625076444606,"_gp_pool_share":false,"_score_pool_share":29.8,"_gate_rev_durability":0.07086825745502345,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":60.4,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.06335313808779197,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":81.5,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.026936032059225012,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":83.7,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.008069525071769867,"_gp_sbc_dilution":true,"_score_sbc_dilution":86.6,"_gate_insider_own":0.04694,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":31.3,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"Cathay General Bancorp operates as the holding company for Cathay Bank that offers various commercial banking products and services to individuals, professionals, and small to medium-sized businesses in the United States. It offers savings accounts, checking accounts, money market deposit accounts, certificates of deposit, individual retirement accounts, and public funds deposits, and acceptance of checking, savings, demand deposits, time deposits, real estate, and consumer loans. The company also provides loan products, such as commercial real estate loans, commercial loans, small business administration loans, residential mortgage loans, real estate construction loans, and home equity lines of credit, and installment loans to individuals for household and other consumer expenditures. In addition, it offers trade financing, letter of credit, wire transfer, foreign currency spot and forward contract, safe deposit, overdraft, cash checking, automatic teller machine, Internet banking, investment, and other customary bank services, as well as investment products and services, such as stocks, bonds, mutual funds, insurance, annuities, and advisory services. The company was formerly known as Cathay Bancorp, Inc. and changed its name to Cathay General Bancorp in November 2003. Cathay General Bancorp was founded in 1962 and is headquartered in Los Angeles, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Chang Ming Liu | CEO, President & Director | Age 58 | Compensation: $2.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $645K ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 6%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $287K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $5K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 3\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (2/10).","financial_summary":["Cathay General Bancorp is a mid-cap financial services business with a $4.3B market cap on $818M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +1% over the past three years and +7% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 12% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business barely earns its keep economically.","The business throws off $364M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 44 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.17\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.3\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and thin 0.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 6.3% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 4.7% of the shares, and within its sector the business captures 1.8\u00d7 its fair share of profits, a structural advantage visible in the numbers."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.4) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.4239766081871352},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 7.8% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $4.1M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Revenue growth lags most Financial Services peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Operating margins 19% above sector median \u2014 the quantitative trace of pricing power","Trading at a 49% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","34 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Financial quality scores above most Financial Services peers","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Cathay General Bancorp (NASDAQ:CATY) Stock Has Consensus Target Price of $62.25","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/09/cathay-general-bancorp-nasdaqcaty-stock-has-consensus-target-price-of-62-25.html","date":"2026-11-09","timestamp":1794217528.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.511,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Cathay General Bancorp Declares $0.38 Per Share Dividend","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/cathay-general-bancorp-declares-0-213000024.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794605400.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.527,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"The Bet Behind Cathay General Bancorp's Rally","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/banks/nasdaq-caty/cathay-general-bancorp/news/the-bet-behind-cathay-general-bancorps-rally","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794551378.399,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.44,"tier":1,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"The Call Cathay Pacific Airways Bulls Got Right","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/hk/transportation/hkg-293/cathay-pacific-airways-shares/news/the-call-cathay-pacific-airways-bulls-got-right","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794608922.092,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment